# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. With core.autocrlf=true (the default on
# Windows) a checkout would otherwise give them CRLF, and `#!/bin/sh` followed
# by a carriage return fails with "bad interpreter" — a broken hook on a fresh
# clone, which is exactly when nobody is looking for one.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
# The same for what runs on the Raspberry Pi: a script, systemd units and an
# environment file, all read on Linux.
deploy/pi/* text eol=lf

# Pictures are bytes, not text: never convert their line endings.
*.png binary

# The icon font and its stylesheet, kept exactly as published — byte for
# byte, so the stylesheet still hashes to the release's own integrity value
# (see "Icon font" in the README).
*.woff2 binary
vendor/tabler/** -text
